<header><p class="st-kicker">county · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Chiny</h1><p class="st-meta">940 CE – 1364 CE (approx.) · capital Chiny</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Ardennes county on the Semois, on whose lands the Cistercian abbey of Orval was founded, before it was absorbed by Luxembourg.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The county emerged in the mid-10th century in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardennes">Ardennes</a>, in the frontier region between the Lotharingian duchies and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. Its first known count, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-of-warcq">Otto of Warcq</a>, built a castle at Chiny on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/semois">Semois</a>, and his descendants extended their lands towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carignan-ardennes">Ivoix</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montmedy">Montmédy</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Chiny was a wooded, thinly settled county of castles, iron working and abbeys. The counts sponsored the abbey of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orval-abbey">Orval</a>, founded in 1070 and later Cistercian, which became the county's main religious centre. They were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of the Empire, connected by marriage to Bar, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-namur">Namur</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borgloon">Loon</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1226 Countess Jeanne married Arnold of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borgloon">Loon</a>, joining Chiny to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-loon">County of Loon</a>. After the Loon line ended, the county was sold in 1364 to Wenceslaus, duke of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-luxembourg">Luxembourg</a>, and merged into the County of Luxembourg; it lies today in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-belgium">Belgium</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="county, 940 CE – 1364 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="